{
  "analysis": "Doom boots and loads the WAD but fails on Z_Malloc because the zone memory is only 600000 bytes instead of the expected 16MB. The custom stdlib has a 1GB static heap in BSS, and basic_malloc should be able to handle large allocations. I need to trace what's happening inside basic_malloc to understand why large allocations fail. I'll add debug tracing to the VM and also get the full basic_malloc disassembly.",
  "plan": "Get the full basic_malloc disassembly, then add tracing to the VM to log basic_malloc calls with size and return value. This will reveal why 16MB allocations fail but ~600KB succeeds.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mips-linux-gnu-objdump -d --start-address=0x439ae8 --stop-address=0x439c70 /app/doomgeneric_mips > /tmp/basic_malloc.txt; cat /tmp/basic_malloc.txt\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
